# Screenshot artefacts — deliberately NOT versioned (2026-07-24).
# PNGs don't delta-compress, so every run writes full new blobs: estate-check captures 134
# full-page shots (~120MB) per run, and one commit measured 64 of 83 changed shots as
# sub-3KB render noise. That is the bulk of a 476MB .git, for images nobody reviews.
# Change detection belongs to the pixel-diff net (which reports only what moved) and to the
# text fingerprints; these stay as local run artefacts for triage.
qa/visual-baselines/
qa/evidence/*/estate-shots/

# Benchmark screenshots — third-party sites, large, regenerable via qa/benchmark-presentation.mjs.
# Same reasoning as estate-shots: PNGs do not delta-compress and nobody diffs them.
qa/research/presentation-shots/
qa/research/page-shots/
